    "diagnostic_outcome": "DIAGNOSED",
    "failure_family": "shared_memory_race",
    "root_cause": "In folded_warp_writes, multiple threads in the same warp write to the same shared memory slots[slot] where slot = threadIdx.x & 15U; with blockDim 32, each slot is targeted by two threads. The writes occur before __syncthreads(), producing a write-after-write hazard on shared memory. The racecheck finding at kernel.cu:11 identifies this shared-memory race.",
    "source_locations": [
      {
        "path": "kernel.cu",
        "line": 11,
        "function": null
      }
    ],
    "recommended_change": "Remove the folded_warp_writes kernel invocation or redesign the shared memory writes so that each shared memory location is written by a single thread before synchronization. If the kernel is only diagnostic test code, avoid launching it during normal vector_add execution.",
